      "content": "<h3>All Comparator methods at a glance</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;\">\n<tr><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Method</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">What it does</th></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>compare(a, b)</strong></td><td>The one abstract method: orders two objects</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Comparator.comparing(keyExtractor)</strong></td><td>Order by a field (any Comparable)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>comparing(keyExtractor, keyComparator)</strong></td><td>Order by a field with your own comparator for it</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>comparingInt / comparingLong / comparingDouble</strong></td><td>Order by a primitive field, no boxing</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>thenComparing(...)</strong></td><td>Tie-breaker when the first order says equal</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>thenComparingInt / Long / Double</strong></td><td>Tie-breaker on a primitive field</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>reversed()</strong></td><td>The opposite order</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Comparator.naturalOrder() / reverseOrder()</strong></td><td>compareTo order / its opposite</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Comparator.nullsFirst(c) / nullsLast(c)</strong></td><td>Handle null elements safely</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Collections.reverseOrder()</strong></td><td>Reverse of the natural order (older style)</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>equals(obj)</strong></td><td>Inherited; rarely used</td></tr>\n</table>"
